---
// The section header eight capabilities were emitting character for character.
//
// MEASURED BEFORE EXTRACTING, not assumed. Across the 21 blocks there are seven
// distinct heading signatures, but they are mostly "does this block have a
// header at all": 6 have none, 4 have an h2 that is CONTENT rather than a
// section header (BuyBox's product title, Guarantee's derived policy fact,
// Hero's headline), and 10 have a real section header. Of those ten, EIGHT
// emitted byte-identical markup — Faq x2, Benefits x2, Comparison x2,
// HowItWorks x2 — differing only in the data expression.
//
// THIS IS A PURE REFACTOR. No new treatment, no alignment prop, no scale, no
// supporting text, no variant. The API is exactly the two values the existing
// markup interpolates and nothing else, because nothing else exists yet.
// Designing an API for treatments we have not justified would be inventing
// variety rather than removing duplication, and this phase only has evidence
// for the second.
//
// IT IS NOT A CAPABILITY. It is not in the registry, not addressable from a
// DesignSpec, and the Design Agent still sees exactly the same 21 capabilities.
// A block composes it; nothing selects it.
//
// THE COPY STAYS WITH THE BLOCK. FAQ_EYEBROW, BENEFITS_EYEBROW,
// COMPARISON_EYEBROW and STEPS_EYEBROW remain where they are: this primitive
// must not learn that "Faq says Preguntas frecuentes". Data belongs to the
// block, presentation belongs here.
interface Props {
  eyebrow: string;
  title: string;
}

const { eyebrow, title } = Astro.props;
---

<p class="text-eyebrow font-bold uppercase text-rust">{eyebrow}</p>
<h2 class="mt-1 text-display md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl">{title}</h2>
